---
import CaseLayout from '../../components/CaseLayout.astro';
---
<CaseLayout
  title="Tain"
  description="A personal diary of everything you have consumed — books, games, movies, trails — ranked by comparison, with notes from you to future you."
  label="Personal Project // Web App"
  cover="/assets/projects/tain/cover.webp"
  coverAlt="Tain — everything you loved, in order"
  meta={[
    { label: 'Role', value: 'Solo, Design &amp; Build' },
    { label: 'Platform', value: 'Installable web app' },
  ]}
  action={{ label: 'Open Tain at tain.paramore.design', href: 'https://tain.paramore.design' }}
>
  <p>
    <strong>Everything you loved, in order.</strong> Tain is a personal diary of everything
    I&rsquo;ve consumed &mdash; books, games, movies, even hiking trails &mdash; ranked by
    comparison rather than by star rating, with notes from me to future me attached to each
    entry. Not a review site, not a social feed. Built because I kept forgetting the things
    I loved. It started life as &ldquo;Ranklist&rdquo;.
  </p>


  <p>
    This one sat as an idea for years before I built it. Getting it working was the easy half.
    The hard half was refusing the first thing the generated design handed back &mdash; it
    functioned, and it felt like nothing. The comparison flow in particular got pulled apart
    and rebuilt until ranking something was genuinely satisfying rather than a chore.
  </p>
</CaseLayout>
